# SHOPFLOW AGILE PROJECT MODEL (.agile-v)

This document serves as the master Agile framework and Product Backlog for the **ShopFlow Multi-Tenant SaaS Platform**. It defines the complete project lifecycle using industry-standard Agile and Scrum methodologies.

---

## 1. AGILE FRAMEWORK OVERVIEW

- **Methodology:** Scrum (2-Week Sprints)
- **Roles:**
  - **Product Owner:** Defines requirements, prioritizes backlog.
  - **Scrum Master:** Facilitates ceremonies, removes blockers.
  - **Development Team:** Full-stack engineers, DevOps, QA.
- **Ceremonies:**
  - Sprint Planning (Day 1)
  - Daily Standup (Daily, 15 mins)
  - Sprint Review (Last Day - Demo to stakeholders)
  - Sprint Retrospective (Last Day - Process improvement)
- **Estimation:** Fibonacci Sequence (1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13) for Story Points.

---

## 2. PRODUCT EPICS

- **EPIC 1:** Foundation & Multi-Tenant Core
- **EPIC 2:** Product Catalog & Inventory
- **EPIC 3:** Point of Sale (POS) & Sales Management
- **EPIC 4:** Customers & CRM
- **EPIC 5:** Supply Chain (Purchases & Suppliers)
- **EPIC 6:** Financials (Payments, Expenses, Invoices)
- **EPIC 7:** Human Resources & Access Control (RBAC)
- **EPIC 8:** Reporting & Business Intelligence
- **EPIC 9:** Notifications & Audit Logs
- **EPIC 10:** Subscriptions & SaaS Billing
- **EPIC 11:** DevOps, Infrastructure & AI

---

## 3. DETAILED SPRINT BACKLOG

### SPRINT 1: Monorepo & Infrastructure Foundation
**Goal:** Establish the technical foundation for the project.
- [x] **Task 1:** Initialize Turborepo with Next.js (Web) and NestJS (API).
- [x] **Task 2:** Setup PostgreSQL and Redis via Docker Compose.
- [x] **Task 3:** Configure Prisma ORM and define base schema.
- [x] **Task 4:** Setup CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions).

### SPRINT 2: Authentication & SaaS Core
**Goal:** Enable secure user login and strict multi-tenant isolation.
- [x] **Story 2.1:** As a user, I can register using my email and password.
- [x] **Story 2.2:** As a user, I can log in and receive a JWT.
- [x] **Story 2.3:** As a business owner, when I register, an Organization is automatically created.
- [x] **Story 2.4:** As a developer, I must ensure API endpoints strictly filter data by `organizationId`.

### SPRINT 3: Product Catalog & Brand Management
**Goal:** Allow users to define the products they sell.
- [ ] **Story 3.1:** As a manager, I can create, update, and delete Categories.
- [ ] **Story 3.2:** As a manager, I can create Brands.
- [ ] **Story 3.3:** As a manager, I can create a Product with a name, SKU, barcode, and base price.
- [ ] **Story 3.4:** As a manager, I can add Product Variants (e.g., Size: Large, Color: Red).

### SPRINT 4: Warehouses & Inventory Tracking
**Goal:** Manage stock levels across different locations.
- [ ] **Story 4.1:** As an owner, I can create multiple Stores and Warehouses.
- [ ] **Story 4.2:** As a manager, I can view current stock levels for any product at any location.
- [ ] **Story 4.3:** As a manager, I can manually adjust stock levels (e.g., for damaged goods).
- [ ] **Story 4.4:** As a manager, I can transfer stock between a Warehouse and a Store.

### SPRINT 5: Point of Sale (POS) Interface
**Goal:** Provide a fast, responsive interface for cashiers to process sales.
- [x] **Story 5.1:** As a cashier, I can search for products by name or barcode scanner.
- [x] **Story 5.2:** As a cashier, I can add items to the cart and see the subtotal, tax, and total.
- [x] **Story 5.3:** As a cashier, I can apply a line-item discount or an overall cart discount.
- [x] **Story 5.4:** As a cashier, I can suspend a sale (hold cart) and retrieve it later.

### SPRINT 6: Sales Transactions & Order Processing
**Goal:** Finalize checkout and guarantee data consistency.
- [ ] **Story 6.1:** As a cashier, I can accept payment via Cash, Card, or Custom method.
- [ ] **Story 6.2:** As the system, I must decrement inventory atomically when a sale is completed.
- [ ] **Story 6.3:** As a cashier, I can print or email a digital receipt.
- [ ] **Story 6.4:** As a manager, I can process a refund and return items to inventory.

### SPRINT 7: Supply Chain & CRM
**Goal:** Track who buys from the business and who the business buys from.
- [ ] **Story 7.1:** As a cashier, I can attach a Customer profile to a POS sale for loyalty tracking.
- [ ] **Story 7.2:** As a manager, I can create Supplier profiles.
- [ ] **Story 7.3:** As a manager, I can generate a Purchase Order and send it to a Supplier.
- [ ] **Story 7.4:** As a manager, I can receive a Purchase Order, which automatically increases inventory.

### SPRINT 8: Financials & Accounting
**Goal:** Track business profitability and cash flow.
- [ ] **Story 8.1:** As an owner, I can log daily operational Expenses (e.g., electricity, salaries).
- [ ] **Story 8.2:** As a B2B user, I can generate an Invoice for a customer and track its payment status (Paid, Unpaid, Overdue).
- [ ] **Story 8.3:** As an owner, I can view a Profit & Loss (P&L) statement based on sales, COGS, and expenses.

### SPRINT 9: Employee Management & RBAC
**Goal:** Manage staff access and shifts.
- [ ] **Story 9.1:** As an owner, I can invite employees via email to join my organization.
- [ ] **Story 9.2:** As an owner, I can assign Roles (Admin, Manager, Cashier) to restrict system access.
- [ ] **Story 9.3:** As an employee, I can clock in and clock out to record my attendance.

### SPRINT 10: Reports & Dashboard Intelligence
**Goal:** Give business owners a bird's-eye view of their operations.
- [ ] **Story 10.1:** As an owner, I can view my daily, weekly, and monthly sales graphs on the Dashboard.
- [ ] **Story 10.2:** As an owner, I can see a "Low Stock Alerts" widget.
- [ ] **Story 10.3:** As a manager, I can generate an end-of-day register closure report.
- [ ] **Story 10.4:** As a manager, I can export reports to CSV or PDF.

### SPRINT 11: Automation, Audit & AI
**Goal:** Implement advanced features and security logging.
- [ ] **Story 11.1:** As a system admin, I can view an Audit Log showing exactly who performed what action.
- [ ] **Story 11.2:** As a user, I receive in-app Notifications for critical events (e.g., Stock out).
- [ ] **Story 11.3:** As an owner, I can ask the AI Assistant natural language queries about my business data.

### SPRINT 12: Production DevOps & SaaS Monetization
**Goal:** Launch the platform globally.
- [ ] **Story 12.1:** As a system admin, I can write Terraform scripts to provision Kubernetes clusters.
- [ ] **Story 12.2:** As a system admin, I can setup Prometheus and Grafana for monitoring.
- [ ] **Story 12.3:** As the platform owner, I can configure Stripe billing for different SaaS tiers (Basic, Pro, Enterprise).
- [ ] **Story 12.4:** As the platform owner, I can use the Super Admin Panel to view overall platform health and tenant counts.

---

## 4. DEFINITION OF DONE (DoD)
A User Story is only considered "Done" when:
1. Code is fully implemented.
2. Code passes TypeScript linting (`npx turbo run lint`).
3. Code compiles successfully (`npx turbo run build`).
4. Automated tests (Unit/Integration) are written and pass.
5. Peer code review is completed.
6. The feature is tested manually and meets all Acceptance Criteria.
7. Feature is deployed to the staging environment without errors.